<title>POLAND: HANDLOWY UP 8.3 PCT ON BOURSE DEBUT.</title>
<headline>HANDLOWY UP 8.3 PCT ON BOURSE DEBUT.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Bank Handlowy SA started trading on the main market of the Warsaw Stock Exchange at 37.9 zlotys, 8.3 percent above its public offering price of 35 zlotys.</p>
<p>The opening came slightly below analysts' predictions centering around 40 zlotys.</p>
<p>The 9.75-million-share retail tranche of the bank's May-June public offering at 35 zlotys each was three times subscribed and the 19.5-million-share institutional tranche was 17.4 times subscribed with foreign demand over $3.5 billion.</p>
<p>The 24-percent long-term investor tranche went to JP Morgan, Zurich Insurance and Swedbank.</p>
<p>The bank's Global Depositary Receipts (GDRs) currently trade on the London bourse.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
